  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Fixes all six retained native-Windows portability failures and two subsequently reproduced cache races in implementation commits ddf11b9fb96bb271165d475a8aaa67849b7428a4, 7b01f95b7097f02b2b6c4e3c29f0bc3fd0d9819a, eeceec19673860fecb33e5de0658d3e81ef94c21, and 42464fc165dd18196b0530a621e43e75675ad314. Atomic cache publication and reads use bounded Windows-only transient-error retries without unlinking a live destination; cleanup ignores only an entry that vanishes with ENOENT after enumeration. Release and native-build fixtures preserve the exact target semantics while using host-native paths and line endings. At exact cb11a887a98e13193a2bdca2814fd62233926a32, the native Windows checkout on official Node.js 26.7.0 passed a clean build, five consecutive 19/19 cache runs, two consecutive three-test heartbeat/FFLAS runs, and the 117/117 focused suite; the physical Apple M1 cache suite passed 19/19. Exact Linux test:changed passed the build, 448-test unit, compiler, and 438-pass/0-fail/3-skip integration tiers, and the separately declared build, compiler, integration, focused, and architecture commands all pass.",
    "risks": [
      "One earlier standalone Linux integration run encountered the unrelated fixed-host dense-integer timing gate; the exact test passed immediately in isolation and the final exact cb11 test:changed integration tier passed 438 tests with 3 skips and no failures.",
      "The broader macOS CI failures previously classified as ASan capability, dense-prime timing, /var source identity, and Linux-x64 fixture assumptions remain separate from this lane."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Integrate the ordered range after db6258674e6f191b8187c31e2231a45c73a5c5c6 once this exact closure is approved.",
      "Resume the separate Windows static-CRT and PDB reproducibility lane on the integrated portable checkpoint."
    ]
  }
